> I've got a wand of speed monster. I've looked at the wand-343.txt, and
> it neither says 'permanent' nor does it say 'for n (more) turns' as with
> other things, so I don't know whether to zap it at myself and stow away
> as I'm then permanently fast (IIRC even faster as I'm wearing speed
> boots), or keep it for emergencies (because it runs out).

Speed monster (or a potion of speed, or a haste self spell) makes you
fast; speed boots make you very fast. You can't get any faster than very
fast, so strictly speaking you need only the boots, but it's convenient
to be intrinsically fast as well in case something happens to your boots.

> So, permanent, or n (more) turns?

Permanent in vanilla, but some events can take your speed away (being
almost-petrified by a cockatrice, a run-in with a skeleton) so it's best
to stow it away where you can get at it.

